__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.msgpack
checkpoints/
wandb/
.venv/

# POLICY (2026-08-28, corrected after round 2's provenance review): CSV
# and JSON results ARE committed - they're small text, and gitignoring
# them made every number from rounds 1/1.5/2 exist on only one laptop,
# an unacceptable single point of failure. Only large/regeneratable
# binaries stay ignored: *.msgpack (checkpoints, rule above - already
# catches results/ckpt/*.msgpack regardless of nesting) and figures/
# (PNGs regeneratable from the committed CSVs + each experiment script's
# own plotting code, so keeping them out of git keeps repo size down).
#
# This required fixing the repo ROOT .gitignore too: it had a bare
# `results/`, which (unlike a rule scoped with a leading slash) matches
# a directory of that name at ANY depth, so it was also catching
# layernorm_study/results/ and made it impossible to ever un-ignore
# anything under it from here (git's directory-exclusion short-circuit
# never descends into an already-excluded directory to check a deeper
# .gitignore's negation) - the root rule is now anchored (/results/),
# scoped to the parent project's own top-level results/ dir only.
figures/*
!figures/.gitkeep
